    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can SAMBAR run with kmin=2 and kmax=9 on exactly six mutation samples while preserving kmax=9?"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "**SAMBAR**. SAMBAR reduces sparse mutation data to pathway-level scores with gene-length and, when configured, patient mutation-burden normalization. Patient distances and subtype labels depend on the downstream clustering settings; they are distinct from gene communities in a regulatory network. This is pathway aggregation followed by distance-based clustering, not non-negative matrix factorization; a mutation score does not establish permanent functional loss or equivalence of every mutation in a pathway.\n\nYou would need somatic mutation matrix, gene/exon-size CSV, cancer-gene list, GMT pathway file. The analysis would provide sample-by-gene mutation scores, not pathway scores; pathway-by-sample mutation scores, not cluster labels; sample-to-cluster labels, separate from score and distance matrices; pairwise sample distances, not cluster labels.\n\nNo files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
